From: Nerves ROCK Pi S maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rock-pi-s: use RK3308 data and disable DMC

Match the known-working Radxa ROCK Pi S Buildroot device tree. The board uses
the RK3308 data rather than the RK3308K variant, and its DMC integration is not
functional. Leaving DMC enabled causes an early firmware call and prevents a
reliable kernel bring-up.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308-rock-pi-s.dts | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308-rock-pi-s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308-rock-pi-s.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308-rock-pi-s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308-rock-pi-s.dts
@@ -7,7 +7,6 @@
 
 #include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
-/* #include "rk3308.dtsi" */
-#include "rk3308k.dtsi"
+#include "rk3308.dtsi"
 
 / {
 	model = "Radxa ROCK Pi S";
@@ -201,7 +200,7 @@ &cpu0 {
 
 &dmc {
 	center-supply = <&vdd_log>;
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &emmc {
-- 
2.43.0
